<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khengarji I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1548–1585</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khengarji I was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jadeja">Jadeja</a> ruler who united Cutch in the mid-16th century and is regarded as the founder of the Cutch State. Raised at the court of the sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, he overcame rival Jadeja kinsmen with their support, took the title Rao and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhuj">Bhuj</a> his capital. His descendants ruled Cutch until its accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948.</p></div>
